1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:12,487
The acquisition table has five signals: pack voltage and current at one hertz, surface temperature at one hertz, ambient temperature at zero point one hertz, and a sequence plus source timestamp on every message.

2
00:00:12,487 --> 00:00:14,502
Current is positive on discharge.

3
00:00:14,502 --> 00:00:20,873
The simulator adds voltage, current, and temperature noise, quantization, and a small packet loss rate.

4
00:00:20,873 --> 00:00:27,257
It also supports a simulation speed multiplier, so a two-hour discharge can be demonstrated in six minutes.

5
00:00:27,257 --> 00:00:31,456
Source time is simulation time; ingest time is wall-clock time.

6
00:00:31,456 --> 00:00:42,827
The assumptions are explicit: cells are balanced, capacity is constant within a run, the OCV curve comes from literature, convection is fixed, and hysteresis is ignored.

7
00:00:42,827 --> 00:00:47,305
The plant uses private parameters; the twin only receives telemetry.

